From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: finalpantasy <finalpantasy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:53:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] GuestHeap: size-class fast path for blocks up to 1,024
 bytes

Growable heaps serve small requests from 64 KiB chunks cut into
16-byte classes. Free lists live in eight lock shards; a freed slot
returns to the shard that created its chunk, and a thread whose own
list is empty steals from the other shards before taking a new chunk.
Each slot's requested size is an atomic, so Size, Free and in-place
ReAlloc are O(1) and a racing double free fails once. A lock-free
insert-only table maps addresses to chunks. Bounded heaps and larger
blocks keep the old path.

Micro-benchmark (WSL, one thread): 162 ns to 44 ns per alloc and free
pair. In FFXII at 120 fps GuestHeap fell from 4.4% to 0.1% of the
game thread's samples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
